      "observed": "reconcile validates gateway/API ingress/status/engine-finished cardinality and body hashes, but does not validate API response.id, engine_request count/settings/config, API-finished count, actual prompt-array hash, prompt/total usage or plan-derived body. analyze stores only the first effective_config and checks only completion usage/text. Rows with reconcile issues still flow into outputs, baselines and comparison.",
      "mutation_evidence": "Six in-memory mutations (wrong response.id, wrong API prompt usage, wrong seed, wrong effective max_num_seqs, duplicate engine_request, missing api_finished) all return [] from reconcile. The actual dataset was independently checked for all these fields and passed.",
      "impact": "verification_issues=[] and input_ids_stable=true alone are weaker than the planned identity/sampling/template evidence contract. Future mixed/corrupt logs can be reported as comparable or become an implicit baseline.",
      "minimal_fix": [
        "Build an exact expected ID->batch/task/body/settings map from plan and validate against all request layers and response.id.",
        "Require one engine_request and one api_finished, recompute prompt-token hash from the full array, validate prompt/completion/total usage and all effective configs rather than retaining only the first.",
        "Separate planned, HTTP accepted, evidence verified, timing eligible and sequence comparable denominators. Preserve failures in planned/accepted counts, but do not let invalid outputs seed a baseline or count as consistent.",
        "Explicitly select the 8 batch-00 direct/concurrency-1 baselines and verify their observed singleton schedule exposure instead of using the first available output for each task."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "interpretation": {
    "independent_counts": "8 singleton baselines, then 136 comparisons = 88 equal + 48 different; mixed-exposed 85 = 37 equal + 48 different; singleton-exposed 59 includes 8 baselines, leaving 51 singleton comparisons, all equal.",
    "input_sampling_template": "For every task, all 18 formal requests have one body hash, identical full actual prompt-token arrays, identical recorded temperature/top_p/top_k/seed/max_tokens/n and one recorded effective configuration. Body reconstruction includes enable_thinking=false and stream=false. This excludes recorded input/template/sampling changes; not all unrecorded runtime factors have been isolated.",
    "temperature_and_seed": "temperature=0 is greedy generation here. seed=17 records a frozen setting, not evidence about random-sampling reproducibility.",
    "batch_definition": "Mixed exposure means at least one CPU scheduler plan for that request contained more than one sequence. This is not a CUDA trace or a persistent batch assignment.",
    "first_divergence_caution": "Each request has one prefill and one scheduled group slot per returned output token, with 7822 weighted slots matching 7822 actual output IDs. Matching CPU step indices, 41 first divergences occur in a mixed plan and 7 in a singleton plan despite earlier mixed exposure; do not assert that the first differing token always occurs in a mixed plan or that a current-step kernel caused it. No cross-request KV/memory/hidden-state or teacher-forced logits probe was performed.",
    "length_and_quality": "54 length finishes remain in the 144; 90 stop finishes. The comparison concerns emitted actual sequences to their cap, not complete-answer quality.",
    "closed_loop": "Eight tasks submitted per batch to a 1/2/4-worker thread pool; later HTTP arrivals wait for a worker. No controlled open-loop offered rate. 24 requests per config, 3 batches per config, all HTTP 200. active=2/waiting=2 is not overflow-tested by a maximum four-client workload; 0 rejections cannot establish overload protection or production capacity.",
    "admission_observation": "Backend API monotonic event overlap peaks are direct=1/2/4 and bounded=1/2/2 across concurrency=1/2/4. Bounds and waiting migration are supported in this run.",
    "latency_definitions": "driver_wait uses local submitted->thread-start, client_response local thread-start->full nonstream JSON read, gateway_wait local arrival->dispatch. Engine queue is initial queue only. No complete response is used as client TTFT. Do not add separate medians or subtract absolute timestamps across hosts.",
    "throughput_scope": "Output totals are direct 1/2/4:1323/1294/1300 and bounded 1/2/4:1323/1282/1300. Concurrency-4 totals are equal at 1300, while request-level sequences and lengths differ. No universal throughput ratio, equal per-request work comparison or causal production-capacity conclusion follows."
  },
